The IT department of Den Hartogh (25 colleagues) works as a single team on the growth and goals of our family business, spread over clusters such as IT Operations, Architecture & Security and Data Integration & Analytics. As a Data Engineer within that last cluster, you help the business proactively achieve its business and financial goals, with data in the broadest sense of the word.
Through applications, dashboarding and ad hoc analytics you modernise our data landscape, and there is plenty of space to innovate with predictive & generic AI, Data Science and Process Automation (RPA). You report directly to the Teamlead Data Integration & Analytics.
What are you gonna do?
- You bridge between organization and processes on the one hand and technology on the other;
- As a sparring partner for the business, you take management information to a higher level, in innovative and complex data projects;
- You maintain and expand our data pipelines in SQL and build a semantic model;
- You perform ad hoc analyses with SQL (and R) and stimulate continuous improvement through data and process analysis;
- You work closely with data professionals to improve the usability of internal and external data.
You are our ideal candidate if you:
- Have a bachelor's degree in Business Engineering, Business IT & Management, Data Science, Analytics or similar;
- Have at least 4 years of experience in a similar position and at least 4 years with SQL;
- Strong in SQL, DAX, dimensional modelling, data vault modeling, version management and Scrum;
- Excellent communicates in Dutch and English (word and writing) and has a sharp, critical look, in addition you dare to abrade the business;
- Being proactive and result-oriented, with a strong drive to keep improving and developing yourself;
- Pré: 2+ years experience with Machine Learning models, advanced Power BI knowledge and experience in implementing AI models in an organization.
What do we offer?
- A salary between € 4,000,- and € 5,400,- gross per month (according to knowledge and experience), plus laptop and telephone of the business, 30 holiday days (e.g. full-time), 8% holiday allowance, a holiday gratification of € 550,- gross, travel allowance and a good pension scheme;
- Entrepreneurship: a challenging function with a high degree of autonomy, flexibility and responsibility, within a growing and informal organisation with ambitious goals;
- Hybrid works from our Basecamp in Rotterdam (at full-time 3 day office, 2 home): a modern working environment overlooking the Waterweg, an inhouse gym, restaurant and the Den Hartogh Academy with over 500 training courses;
- An international but familiar working environment, with relevant colleagues from all over the world;
- Eye for each other: a fine working atmosphere, a caring and vitality budget and access to Benefits at Work with attractive discounts.
Enthusiastic?
Do you recognize yourself in this role and would you like to help shape our data landscape? Apply directly via the application button. Any questions? Contact Angel Alemawor, interim corporate recruiter, via +31 6 11804991 or .
