Do you not only want to build frontend solutions, but also guide how we develop our websites and digital platforms in the coming years?
What you need to know about us?
We are Athora Netherlands, an insurance company with the well-known brands Swiss life and Reaal. We mainly deal with pensions and life insurance on the Dutch market. We do so as part of a European group with branches in Ireland, the United Kingdom, Belgium, Germany and Italy. We are a strong company with over one million customers and we want to grow into one of the most important players in the rapidly changing pension market in the coming years. That is why we are looking for people who do not back down to change, who know how to tackle, who have the ambition to deliver results and who therefore get the best out of themselves and their team. Smarter together, we call that.
What are you gonna do?
For our Websites & Portals Platform team we are looking for an experienced frontend engineer that combines technical leadership with strong hands-on knowledge of Angular. Someone who looks forward, can set up a front-end vision and roadmap and take other teams with him in the technical direction.
So you're not just the one who can solve complex front-end issues. You also help determine where we are going, what technical choices we make and how different development teams work together within that course.
As Senior Frontend Engineer / Technical Lead, you will play a central role in the further development of our frontend platform.
One of the things you do is:
- drawing up and promoting the technical vision and frontend roadmap;
- developing and modernising the front-end platform;
- developing reusable platform components for our websites and digital customer environments;
- making and monitoring technical and architectural choices;
- develop hands-on with Angular and TypeScript;
- giving substance to developers and developers using the platform;
- monitoring standards, quality, maintenance and coherence;
- translating needs from different teams into future-proof technical solutions;
- collaborate with, among others, solutions teams, architecture, security and infrastructure.
This involves more than developing software. You help determine the technical course of the front end landscape and ensure that that course actually lands within the organization. What makes this role interesting? You get the chance to impact on multiple levels. One day, you're gonna dive into technology. The other time you discuss an architectural choice, work on the roadmap or help another team to put a solution in the platform. You look beyond the individual issue. You keep wondering: how do we make the platform simpler, more consistent, more scalable and more future-proof?
#LI-DNI
What do we ask of you?
We specifically seek an experienced front-end professional who combines technical depth with vision and leadership.
You have:
- extensive experience with front end development;
- in-depth experience with Angular and TypeScript;
- experience with NX workspace/monorepo and NodeJS, or similar modern frontend environments;
- experience with Azure App Service and Azure Pipelines, or similar cloud and CI/CD environments;
- experience in designing and developing frontend platforms;
- the ability to draw up and implement a technical vision and roadmap;
- experience in guiding developers or other development teams;
- sufficient seniority to explain technical choices and include different stakeholders;
- knowledge of .NET and API integrations (pre);
- experience with Agile, Scrum and/or SAFE;
- minimum HBO work and thinking levels;
- a good mastery of Dutch and English and living in the Netherlands.
Who are you? You're technically strong, but you're not someone who prefers code alone.
- You look beyond today's issue;
- You can see dependencies between teams and systems;
- You dare to make technical choices and stand before them;
- You can enthusiaze and take with you developers;
- You easily switch between developers, architects and management;
- You are pragmatic and know when a solution is technically good enough;
- You take ownership of the platform's development.
You combine the qualities of a senior engineer, technical sparring partner and tractor.
What do we owe you?
You get about 900 colleagues who all think they work at a special company. You will have the opportunity to make an important contribution to the socially relevant theme of pensions. We make sure your pension is well arranged so you can enjoy your old age carefree.
You get the chance to really make a difference when it comes to sustainability, because we've been showing the tone in our business operations and investments for years. Of course you get a (flexible) workplace at our office in Amsterdam that belongs to the best 7% of the world, really. And because you will also work regularly at home, you will receive a budget to properly decorate your homework spot.
In exchange for your commitment, talent and skills, you will receive a holiday allowance and a holiday allowance plus a thirteenth month, 27 holiday days (for a 36-hour contract) and an OV-card or travel allowance for the days you come to the office. And, not unimportant to us, you get a good education budget so you can continue to develop yourself. This gives you the chance to grow, within our company or beyond.
Salary per month:
Based on collective agreement scale 16 HAY, the range is €5.082,02 to € 6.776,03 based on 36 hours.
Enthusiastic?
Reply quickly via the application button!
